{"id":"ENT-2060","title":"Bootstrap resume: partial-progress subset resume and a sync-mode route","description":"Fast-follow to <issue id="ca35a5b4-c595-4ffd-bf20-b7c1fd3dd331" href="https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/ENT-2054/interrupted-batched-bootstrap-can-never-resume-the-resume-ref">ENT-2054</issue> (git-sync PR <pull-request id="a5a95ace-ea35-4645-9155-7740626b4168" href="https://linear.app/entirehq/review/route-replicate-to-bootstrap-when-a-resume-marker-survives-on-the-d7cd09c480fb">entireio/git-sync#116</pull-request>). That PR makes an interrupted batched bootstrap resumable from its `refs/gitsync/bootstrap/*` marker under replicate, but two shapes remain outside the resume route — both surfaced and confirmed by the PR's code review.

## 1. Partial-progress resume (the sharpened remainder of the original wedge)

`replicateBootstrapRoute` requires **all** desired target refs to be absent, because `BuildBootstrapPlans` refuses targets whose desired refs exist. A multi-branch bootstrap interrupted **after any branch finalized** (trunk done, secondary branch mid-flight) therefore can never resume batching: the remaining branch goes as one unsubdividable replicate pack. The live marker is preserved and anchors the delta (PR #116's prune guard), so the pack shrinks relative to a fresh transfer — but if the residual delta exceeds the target's pack cap, the repo wedges exactly like <issue id="ca35a5b4-c595-4ffd-bf20-b7c1fd3dd331" href="https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/ENT-2054/interrupted-batched-bootstrap-can-never-resume-the-resume-ref">ENT-2054</issue>.

Fix shape: subset bootstrap — when a live marker exists and *some* desired refs are absent, route only the absent subset through the bootstrap strategy (existing target refs already serve as haves via `completedRefs`). Needs decisions on mixed-run semantics: what the Result reports, that prune is skipped for the run, and that present branches stay stale until the next delivery (a dormant upstream means no next delivery — consider a follow-up kick).

## 2. Sync mode has no resume route at all

The routing lives in the replicate-only syncer method; `sync --all-refs --prune` against a marker-bearing target still disqualifies bootstrap via `planner.CanBootstrapRelay` (prune disables it outright, `relay.go`). Same wedge shape as the original ticket, different mode. PR #116 only fixed sync mode's destructive half (its prune no longer deletes live markers, via the shared `addPruneCandidates` exception). Wants the marker routing hoisted somewhere both modes share — likely the planner.

Related: sync mode also still labels a resume `empty-target-managed-refs` (`syncer.go:953`), so the new `relay_reason` signal never reaches `sync` — the routing hoist should fix the label with it.

## 3. Batched cutover deletes its temp ref on a create it cannot confirm — highest priority item here

`bootstrap.go` cutover (~`:687`) deletes the temp ref unconditionally, while the branch create rides the preceding best-effort push. Under `BestEffort` the pusher swallows a per-ref `ng` and returns nil (`gitproto/push.go:453-470`, via `OnRejection`), so a rejected create still reaches the delete — destroying the resume position for a branch that was never created, and reporting the run as a success.

**Pre-existing, not a regression:** the cutover delete is byte-identical on `origin/main` (`bootstrap.go:654` there) and untouched by PR #116's diff. Recorded here so nobody bisects it to that PR.

**Empirically confirmed** (independently reproduced, not just read): 80-commit source, `TargetMaxPackBytes=350_000`, 8 batches all pushed successfully, target refuses only the branch create.

```
err=<nil> relayMode="bootstrap-batch" batching=true batches=8
after run: branch present=false  marker present=false
```

Eight batches of work reported as a success, with nothing to show for it and no way back. Reproducer (drop into `internal/syncer` as a `_test.go`, delete after — it asserts a bug, so it must not be committed):

```go
func TestProbeBatchedCutoverLosesMarker(t *testing.T) {
	sourceRepo, sourceFS := newSourceRepo(t)
	makeLargeCommits(t, sourceRepo, sourceFS, 80, 5_000)
	targetRepo, _ := git.Init(memory.NewStorage())
	sourceServer := newSmartHTTPRepoServerV2(t, sourceRepo)
	targetServer := newSmartHTTPRepoServer(t, targetRepo)
	defer sourceServer.Close()
	defer targetServer.Close()

	branchRef := plumbing.NewBranchReferenceName(testBranch)
	tempRef := planner.BootstrapTempRef(branchRef)

	// A returned report short-circuits the test server before it applies ANY
	// command, so apply everything except the branch create by hand, then
	// report ng for that one. Without this the temp ref never advances and the
	// probe measures the wrong thing.
	targetServer.receivePackHook = func(req *packp.UpdateRequests, _ bool) *packp.ReportStatus {
		denied := false
		for _, cmd := range req.Commands {
			if cmd.Name == branchRef {
				denied = true
				continue
			}
			if cmd.New.IsZero() {
				_ = targetRepo.Storer.RemoveReference(cmd.Name)
			} else {
				_ = targetRepo.Storer.SetReference(plumbing.NewHashReference(cmd.Name, cmd.New))
			}
		}
		deny := []plumbing.ReferenceName{"refs/nonexistent/none"}
		if denied {
			deny = []plumbing.ReferenceName{branchRef}
		}
		return syncertest.DenyRefsReport(req, "deny creating a protected branch", deny...)
	}

	result, err := Bootstrap(context.Background(), Config{
		Source: Endpoint{URL: sourceServer.RepoURL()},
		Target: Endpoint{URL: targetServer.RepoURL()},
		AllRefs: true, BestEffort: true,
		ProtocolMode: protocolModeAuto, TargetMaxPackBytes: 350_000,
	})
	_, branchErr := targetRepo.Reference(branchRef, true)
	_, markerErr := targetRepo.Reference(tempRef, true)
	t.Logf("err=%v batches=%d branch=%v marker=%v", err, result.BatchCount, branchErr == nil, markerErr == nil)
}
```

**This is the higher-consequence half of the hazard PR #116 fixed.** Batched is the *large-repo* path — <issue id="5b7a6b15-b273-4116-a4a4-0c2147883e72" href="https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/ENT-1948/mirror-sync-permanently-fails-when-catch-up-pack-exceeds-10-gib">ENT-1948</issue>, the >10 GiB case the whole effort exists for — so a lost resume position here costs a full re-transfer of exactly the repos that can least afford one. `bootstrap --all-refs --target-max-pack-bytes=N` against a target that refuses the create loses an entire batched import, silently, reported as success.

Reachable from the CLI: `--all-refs` implies `BestEffort` for `bootstrap` (`cmd/git-sync/bootstrap.go:68`) and `sync` (`syncplan.go:121`), and `client.go:133` passes `Policy.BestEffort` through for any mode.

**PR #116's fix does not port.** That one dropped strategy-side cleanup and let prune own the marker; here that would leave a *permanent* marker, because `Bootstrap()` rejects `--prune` outright (the `"bootstrap does not support --prune"` guard) — no cleaner would ever exist on that path. The batched path needs the rejection actually threaded into the strategy instead. The syncer already records it (the `rejections` map on `syncSession`, populated from the pusher's `OnRejection` callback), so this is a `bootstrap.Params` field away rather than a redesign: delete the temp ref only when the branch create was not rejected.

(Guards are named rather than cited by line: PR #116 shifted these by ~100 lines and they will move again.)

## Smaller items to sweep into whichever change touches the area

* Stale marker under `Mappings` **or branch-scoped prune has no cleaner**: `PruneTarget` only selects `RefKindOther` under AllRefs-without-Mappings, so an interrupted `--map` run leaves a marker that lingers forever (it no longer misroutes anything after PR #116's orphan fix — it just persists). This also means the prune backstop PR #116 relies on doesn't exist under those scopes.
* **Dry-run doesn't disclose marker lifecycle** (consistent with the batched temp-ref lifecycle, which dry-run also omits) — fold in if plan reporting is touched.
* **Reviewer suggestion**: the non-batchable-source integration test asserts the marker survives but not that it was sent as a fetch have; add the assertion if the test server grows negotiation capture.
* **Testing gotcha for whoever picks this up**: a non-nil `receivePackHook` report short-circuits the integration test server *before* it applies any command, so a hook that denies indiscriminately makes marker-lifecycle assertions vacuous. Pass ref-only pushes through (`hasPack == false` → return nil) — see `TestRun_IntegrationResumeMarkerSurvivesBestEffortRejectedCreate`.","priority":{"value":0,"name":"No priority"},"url":"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/ENT-2060/bootstrap-resume-partial-progress-subset-resume-and-a-sync-mode-route","gitBranchName":"nodo/ent-2060-bootstrap-resume-partial-progress-subset-resume-and-a-sync","createdAt":"2026-08-28T15:36:30.292Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-31T08:40:47.271Z","archivedAt":null,"completedAt":null,"startedAt":null,"canceledAt":null,"dueDate":null,"slaStartedAt":null,"slaMediumRiskAt":null,"slaHighRiskAt":null,"slaBreachesAt":null,"status":"Backlog","statusType":"backlog","labels":["Bug"],"attachments":[{"id":"aac56297-7e05-411c-afb1-1fb2007b7d55","title":"git-sync PR #116","subtitle":null,"url":"https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/116"}],"documents":[],"stateHistory":[{"state":{"id":"8e117581-93c5-4ca8-b53b-8fc6d2c7510f","name":"Backlog","type":"backlog"},"startedAt":"2026-08-28T15:36:30.292Z","endedAt":null}],"createdBy":"Andrea Nodari","createdById":"76f6927c-ac03-4620-9454-a3acd751fbd7","team":"Entire","teamId":"832db0be-d9d8-45dc-9774-7f35babe62c0","relations":{"blocks":[],"blockedBy":[],"relatedTo":[{"id":"ENT-1948","title":"Mirror sync permanently fails when catch-up pack exceeds 10 GiB receive-pack body cap"},{"id":"ENT-2054","title":"Interrupted batched bootstrap can never resume: the resume ref disqualifies the bootstrap route"}],"duplicateOf":null}}

